This is the production C++23 engine, derived from the local Ninja snapshot:
4e4df1e567eb3c1475a51af261cba2bfff60b4be.

The upstream reference tree is not bundled. sninja is compiled from this
engine; it does not invoke a separate Ninja executable to perform builds.
Original Apache-2.0 notices and COPYING are preserved.

Changes with behavioral/performance significance:
* lexer.{cc,in.cc,h}, scan.h, manifest_path.h, manifest_parser.{cc,h}:
  bounded SIMD runs and borrowed literal paths, deferred variable evaluation,
  canonical path fast path with the original normalizer as fallback.
* state.{cc,h}, object_arena.h: stable owning slabs, single-probe interning.
* pointer_vector.h, graph.h: one inline pointer per graph adjacency; the layout
  remains three machine words. Large lists grow by 1.5x to limit unused space.
  Iterator consumers use inferred iterator types.
* eval_env.{cc,h}: sorted compact bindings, switching to a hash table at 16
  entries to avoid quadratic behavior in large scopes.
* hash_map.h, disk_interface.{cc,h}: owning directory hash caches.
* util.cc: C++23 resize_and_overwrite for direct Windows file reads, plus internal
  stdio opens made non-inheritable at creation on Windows (CRT N mode) so async
  process creation cannot race the old open-then-clear-inheritance sequence.
* graph.cc: inline single-output scan cache and borrowed command input paths.
  The CLI's conservative no-work probe reuses the output dirty cache, checks the
  static DAG before logged leaf inputs, and avoids materializing dependency
  adjacency for a proven no-op. Default API calls restore node state; CLI misses
  can reuse physical stat results only when no dyndep can introduce producers.
  Synthetic phony mtimes are rolled back, and cached missing leaves retain the
  dirtiness invariant expected by the original scanner. Explain mode and
  unsupported states use the complete engine. SNINJA_NOOP_PROBE=0 disables it.
* subprocess.{h,win32.cc}, real_command_runner.cc: directly inheritable child
  pipe endpoints, one shared NUL input handle, adaptive single-worker launch
  pipeline preserving all parent-inheritable handles, acquire/release IOCP
  publication, exact cancellation completion draining, and constant-time removal.
  Captured output is moved into the build result. POSIX shares the movable
  command/output interfaces but retains its original process backend.
* metrics.{h,cc}: thread-safe registration, process launch/wait measurements.
* deps_log.{h,cc}: bounded whole-block reads from the signature onward, avoiding
  stdio tail refills; block-rounded storage is capped at 576 KiB. Partial legacy
  version writes preserve original truncated-header diagnostics. Borrowed record
  payloads, one-pass
  ID validation, alignment-safe word reads and corruption recovery; compact
  32-bit dependency IDs with header and array in one allocation, table views
  surviving reallocation and explicitly rebound after recompaction, and owned
  record cleanup. IDs are resolved directly into graph input slots; missing-deps
  inspection also consumes the indexed view without temporary pointer arrays.
  Reusable contiguous write records keep the same per-record flush boundaries
  for the active append log. Recompaction buffers its private temporary file
  and checks close errors before replacement. Retained dependency arrays are
  remapped in place only after successful replacement, avoiding a second copy;
  failed writes/replacements restore original node IDs and in-memory records.
  SNINJA_RECOMPACT_FLUSH=1 restores per-record flushing during recompaction.
  Recovery offsets and history counters are wide enough for large logs; Windows
  Truncate uses _chsize_s without a narrowing long cast and opens non-inheritable
  handles. A standalone sparse-file check covers actual recovery above 2 GiB.
* ninja.cc: scheduling history is parsed only after a no-op proof misses, still
  before the original scan so dyndep output ordering keeps its prior semantics.
  Early flag exits skip unused default parallelism queries; help and continuing
  commands retain the original default calculation.
* build_log.cc: bounded integral from_chars parsing for ordinary fields with
  the original CRT parsers as fallback for unusual spellings and overflow.
  History lookups borrow output paths, allocating ownership only for new keys;
  history and unique-entry counters are 64-bit.
* clparser.{h,cc}: borrowed line views, allocation-free include-prefix matching,
  filename-suffix checks and ASCII-insensitive system-path matching; include
  strings are moved into the owning set.
* includes_normalize-win32.cc: stream component comparisons and copy the
  unmatched suffix directly, preserving empty final components. Already-normal
  full drive paths avoid a second absolute-path conversion. UNC/unusual paths
  retain the original conversion fallback.
* subprocess.{h,win32.cc}: optional SNINJA_PROFILE_JOBS instrumentation reads
  direct-child process times from handles without changing command lines.
  The default build omits the trace storage and code.
* status_test.cc: include the current status printer/build interfaces so the
  previously unregistered status tests can run.

Build source lists are shared by CMake and configure.py in cmake/engine-*.txt.
Both default to dynamic Windows CRT linkage; configure.py --runtime static and
CMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY=MultiThreaded select static linkage explicitly.
Static CRT has not shown a consistent startup advantage in the latest paired
measurements and regressed some log rewrite workloads, so it remains optional.
SNINJA_PCH (CMake) and configure.py --pch (Clang/MSVC) optionally precompile
standard headers for this engine's own compilation, including bootstrap seeds.
MSVC compiles getopt.c as C++ consistently with the CMake build.
Generated lexer.cc and lexer.in.cc carry the same hand-maintained fast paths.
Future lexer regeneration must retain those fast paths.

The previous independent experiment is retained in src/core, src/simd and
src/cli. Enable SNINJA_BUILD_LEGACY to build it; it is not the default engine.
